From f07d41ae5353d1734471f2da9441431f8b07a505 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nolen Johnson <johnsonnolen@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 01 Oct 2026 00:53:11 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Launcher3: Treat built-in secondary displays like the primary display

* Upstream treats every non-default display as an external monitor,
  giving built-in secondary panels a large screen profile, the
  connected display taskbar and no all apps button in the secondary
  launcher.

* Exclude TYPE_INTERNAL displays from that, so they get a regular
  3-button navigation bar and a usable secondary launcher.

* Also hide recents when the secondary launcher receives a home
   intent, as no transition hides it when recents was opened on top of it.

* Don't create the connected display taskbar UI controller before the
  user is unlocked, as built-in secondary displays exist from boot and
  the home activity can't be resolved until then.

Assisted-by: LLM
Change-Id: I3c1f5b0e7a9d24c86f1e0b5a7d3c9e2f4a6b8d10
---

